IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp3-nouns`
IMPORT `cp3-minimum-qualifying-period`

-- Tests of cp3-minimum-qualifying-period.l4 (subsections 44(2) to 44(5)). Expected values are worked by hand from the text.
-- The basic exemption is 3500 in every year of these tests.

GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      months IS A NUMBER
      earnings IS A NUMBER
      upe IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
`a test year` year months earnings upe MEANS
    `cp3 Year in a contributory period` WITH
        `calendar year of the contributory period` IS year
        `months of that year in the contributory period` IS months
        `earnings on which a base contribution was made for that year` IS earnings
        `basic exemption for that year` IS 3500
        `base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year` IS upe

-- a run of years, oldest first, each of 12 months, all with the same earnings
GIVEN count IS A NUMBER
      start IS A NUMBER
      earnings IS A NUMBER
      upe IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
`a run of test years` count start earnings upe MEANS
    IF count AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE (`a test year` start 12 earnings upe) FOLLOWED BY (`a run of test years` (count MINUS 1) (start PLUS 1) earnings upe)

§ `Tests -- section 44(2)(a)`

-- a year counts if the earnings are not less than the basic exemption
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a) — base contributions were made for a year on earnings not less than the basic exemption` (`a test year` 2020 12 3500 0)
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a) — base contributions were made for a year on earnings not less than the basic exemption` (`a test year` 2020 12 5000 0)
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a) — base contributions were made for a year on earnings not less than the basic exemption` (`a test year` 2020 12 3499.99 0)

-- (i): six years 2015 to 2020; earnings 5000, 3499, 3500, 0, 4000, 6000: four of the six count (3500 is "not less than")
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(i) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` (LIST (`a test year` 2015 12 5000 0), (`a test year` 2016 12 3499 0), (`a test year` 2017 12 3500 0), (`a test year` 2018 12 0 0), (`a test year` 2019 12 4000 0), (`a test year` 2020 12 6000 0))
-- one short of the exemption in 2017: three of the six
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(i) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` (LIST (`a test year` 2015 12 5000 0), (`a test year` 2016 12 3499 0), (`a test year` 2017 12 3499 0), (`a test year` 2018 12 0 0), (`a test year` 2019 12 4000 0), (`a test year` 2020 12 6000 0))
-- only the last six are looked at: eight years, the first four count and the last four do not: two of the last six
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(i) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` (append (`a run of test years` 4 2010 5000 0) (`a run of test years` 4 2014 0 0))
-- fewer than six years: three years, all counting: three is not four
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(i) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` (`a run of test years` 3 2018 5000 0)
-- four years, all counting: four years
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(i) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` (`a run of test years` 4 2017 5000 0)
-- five years, four counting
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(i) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` (append (`a run of test years` 4 2016 5000 0) (`a run of test years` 1 2020 0 0))
-- a year with no month in the contributory period is not "included": 2015 to 2020 and a 2021 with no months and high earnings: the last six included are 2015 to 2020 (3 counting): not four
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(i) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` (LIST (`a test year` 2015 12 0 0), (`a test year` 2016 12 5000 0), (`a test year` 2017 12 5000 0), (`a test year` 2018 12 5000 0), (`a test year` 2019 12 0 0), (`a test year` 2020 12 0 0), (`a test year` 2021 0 9000 0))
-- a year partly in the contributory period (1 month) is included
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(i) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` (LIST (`a test year` 2017 12 5000 0), (`a test year` 2018 12 5000 0), (`a test year` 2019 12 5000 0), (`a test year` 2020 1 5000 0))

-- (i.1): 25 counting years: the last six all count: yes; 24 counting years: no
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least 25 calendar years, three of them in the last six` (`a run of test years` 25 1990 5000 0)
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least 25 calendar years, three of them in the last six` (`a run of test years` 24 1990 5000 0)
-- 25 counting years then 4 not counting: only two of the last six count
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least 25 calendar years, three of them in the last six` (append (`a run of test years` 25 1980 5000 0) (`a run of test years` 4 2005 0 0))
-- 25 counting years then 3 not counting: three of the last six count
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least 25 calendar years, three of them in the last six` (append (`a run of test years` 25 1980 5000 0) (`a run of test years` 3 2005 0 0))

-- (ii): an earlier disability benefit stopped in June 2015: each included year from 2015 on must count
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for each year after the month of cessation of the previous disability benefit` (`a run of test years` 6 2015 5000 0) (JUST (YMD 2015 6 1))
-- 2016 does not count
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for each year after the month of cessation of the previous disability benefit` (append (`a run of test years` 1 2015 5000 0) (append (`a run of test years` 1 2016 0 0) (`a run of test years` 4 2017 5000 0))) (JUST (YMD 2015 6 1))
-- the year of the cessation month (2015) is a year the limb covers (read inclusively, fork F13): with earnings below the exemption in 2015 the limb fails
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for each year after the month of cessation of the previous disability benefit` (append (`a run of test years` 1 2015 0 0) (`a run of test years` 5 2016 5000 0)) (JUST (YMD 2015 6 1))
-- a year before the cessation need not count
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for each year after the month of cessation of the previous disability benefit` (append (`a run of test years` 1 2014 0 0) (`a run of test years` 6 2015 5000 0)) (JUST (YMD 2015 6 1))
-- no earlier benefit: the limb does not apply
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for each year after the month of cessation of the previous disability benefit` (`a run of test years` 6 2015 5000 0) NOTHING
-- no included year after the cessation: every one of none counts
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for each year after the month of cessation of the previous disability benefit` (`a run of test years` 2 2010 0 0) (JUST (YMD 2015 6 1))

-- all three together: (i) false, (i.1) false, (ii) true
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a disability pension` (`a run of test years` 6 2015 5000 0) (JUST (YMD 2015 6 1))
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a disability pension` (`a run of test years` 4 2017 5000 0) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a disability pension` (`a run of test years` 3 2018 5000 0) NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a disability pension` (`a run of test years` 25 1990 5000 0) NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 44(2)(b)`

-- Arguments: month, date of birth, month determined disabled, excluded for disability, the month the benefit is payable for, family allowance recipient, the year's base unadjusted pensionable earnings, the basic exemption.
-- born 10 March 1990: 18 deemed 1 April 2008; determined disabled in May 2020
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(b) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a disability pension` (YMD 2008 3 1) (YMD 1990 3 10) (YMD 2020 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(b) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a disability pension` (YMD 2008 4 1) (YMD 1990 3 10) (YMD 2020 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(b) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a disability pension` (YMD 2020 5 1) (YMD 1990 3 10) (YMD 2020 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(b) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a disability pension` (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 1990 3 10) (YMD 2020 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500
-- excluded by reason of disability
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(b) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a disability pension` (YMD 2015 5 1) (YMD 1990 3 10) (YMD 2020 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2020 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500
-- a family allowance month in a year with earnings below the basic exemption, for a benefit payable after December 1977: left out
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(b) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a disability pension` (YMD 2015 5 1) (YMD 1990 3 10) (YMD 2020 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 6 1) TRUE 3000 3500
-- earnings equal to the basic exemption: not "less than", so the month stays
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(b) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a disability pension` (YMD 2015 5 1) (YMD 1990 3 10) (YMD 2020 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2020 6 1) TRUE 3500 3500
-- a benefit payable for a month in December 1977: the exclusion does not apply
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(b) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a disability pension` (YMD 1975 5 1) (YMD 1950 3 10) (YMD 1977 11 1) FALSE (YMD 1977 12 1) TRUE 3000 3500
-- born 15 June 1940: 18 deemed on 1 July 1958, before 1966: the period starts January 1966
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(b) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a disability pension` (YMD 1965 12 1) (YMD 1940 6 15) (YMD 1980 5 1) FALSE (YMD 1980 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(b) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a disability pension` (YMD 1966 1 1) (YMD 1940 6 15) (YMD 1980 5 1) FALSE (YMD 1980 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500

§ `Tests -- sections 44(2.1) and 44(2.2)`

-- the year's earnings are less than the Year's Basic Exemption: 3500 x 6 / 12 = 1750
#ASSERT `s 44(2.1) — the basic exemption for the year in which a late applicant would have been considered to have become disabled` 3500 2000 6 EQUALS 1750
-- earnings equal to or above it: the Year's Basic Exemption stands
#ASSERT `s 44(2.1) — the basic exemption for the year in which a late applicant would have been considered to have become disabled` 3500 3500 6 EQUALS 3500
#ASSERT `s 44(2.1) — the basic exemption for the year in which a late applicant would have been considered to have become disabled` 3500 4000 6 EQUALS 3500

-- Arguments: a late applicant, became disabled in a family allowance month, the child reached seven in the year, the year's earnings, the basic exemption, the counterfactual.
#ASSERT `s 44(2.2) — a late applicant is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` TRUE TRUE TRUE 2000 3500 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2.2) — a late applicant is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` FALSE TRUE TRUE 2000 3500 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2.2) — a late applicant is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` TRUE FALSE TRUE 2000 3500 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2.2) — a late applicant is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` TRUE TRUE FALSE 2000 3500 TRUE
-- earnings equal to the basic exemption are not "less than" it
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2.2) — a late applicant is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` TRUE TRUE TRUE 3500 3500 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2.2) — a late applicant is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` TRUE TRUE TRUE 2000 3500 FALSE

§ `Tests -- section 44(3)`

-- a third of the years and at least three: 4 years of 12 (12 >= 12)
#ASSERT `s 44(3)(a) — base contributions were made for at least one third of the years, and for at least three years` 4 12
-- 3 of 12: a quarter, under a third
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(3)(a) — base contributions were made for at least one third of the years, and for at least three years` 3 12
-- 3 of 3: a third and three years
#ASSERT `s 44(3)(a) — base contributions were made for at least one third of the years, and for at least three years` 3 3
-- 2 of 3: not three years, although more than a third
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(3)(a) — base contributions were made for at least one third of the years, and for at least three years` 2 3
-- 1 of 1: more than a third but not three years
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(3)(a) — base contributions were made for at least one third of the years, and for at least three years` 1 1
-- 3 of 9: exactly a third
#ASSERT `s 44(3)(a) — base contributions were made for at least one third of the years, and for at least three years` 3 9
-- 4 of 13: 12 < 13: under a third
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(3)(a) — base contributions were made for at least one third of the years, and for at least three years` 4 13
#ASSERT `s 44(3)(b) — base contributions were made for at least ten years` 10
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(3)(b) — base contributions were made for at least ten years` 9

-- born 15 June 1950: 65 on 15 June 2015. Years 2005 to 2008 with earnings above the exemption (4 years), 2009 to 2015 below (7 years), 2016 to 2020 below (5 years, after the year of the 65th birthday: left out).
-- The years in the total: 2005 to 2015: 11. A base contribution in 4 of them: 4 x 3 = 12 >= 11. Without leaving the five years out it would be 16 and 12 < 16.
#ASSERT count (`s 44(3)(a) — the calendar years in the total, leaving out the years after 65 in which the earnings do not exceed the basic exemption` (append (`a run of test years` 4 2005 5000 5000) (append (`a run of test years` 7 2009 1000 1000) (`a run of test years` 5 2016 1000 1000))) (YMD 1950 6 15)) EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `s 44(3) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a death benefit, a survivor's pension and an orphan's benefit` (append (`a run of test years` 4 2005 5000 5000) (append (`a run of test years` 7 2009 1000 1000) (`a run of test years` 5 2016 1000 1000))) (YMD 1950 6 15)
-- the same record without the five low years after 65 removed would fail (16 years, 4 contributions): the same years but the contributor born in 1980 (65 in 2045, so nothing is left out)
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(3) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a death benefit, a survivor's pension and an orphan's benefit` (append (`a run of test years` 4 2005 5000 5000) (append (`a run of test years` 7 2009 1000 1000) (`a run of test years` 5 2016 1000 1000))) (YMD 1980 6 15)
-- the year of the 65th birthday itself is not "after" it: 2015 with earnings below the exemption stays in the total
#ASSERT count (`s 44(3)(a) — the calendar years in the total, leaving out the years after 65 in which the earnings do not exceed the basic exemption` (`a run of test years` 2 2015 1000 1000) (YMD 1950 6 15)) EQUALS 1
-- born 20 December 1950: 65 on 20 December 2015 (the actual birthday: paragraph 44(3)(a) is outside section 2(2)); 2016 and 2017 are after the year of reaching 65
#ASSERT count (`s 44(3)(a) — the calendar years in the total, leaving out the years after 65 in which the earnings do not exceed the basic exemption` (`a run of test years` 3 2015 1000 1000) (YMD 1950 12 20)) EQUALS 1
-- a year after 65 with earnings above the exemption stays
#ASSERT count (`s 44(3)(a) — the calendar years in the total, leaving out the years after 65 in which the earnings do not exceed the basic exemption` (`a run of test years` 3 2015 5000 5000) (YMD 1950 12 20)) EQUALS 3
-- ten years of contributions in forty years: paragraph (b)
#ASSERT `s 44(3) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a death benefit, a survivor's pension and an orphan's benefit` (append (`a run of test years` 10 1980 5000 5000) (`a run of test years` 30 1990 1000 1000)) (YMD 1990 6 15)
-- nine years of 40: neither
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(3) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a death benefit, a survivor's pension and an orphan's benefit` (append (`a run of test years` 9 1980 5000 5000) (`a run of test years` 31 1989 1000 1000)) (YMD 1990 6 15)
-- a base contribution is deemed made only when the earnings EXCEED the exemption: 12 years of earnings equal to it
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(3) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a death benefit, a survivor's pension and an orphan's benefit` (`a run of test years` 12 1990 3500 3500) (YMD 1990 6 15)

§ `Tests -- sections 44(4) and 44(5)`

#ASSERT `s 44(4)(a) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` (`a run of test years` 6 2015 5000 0)
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(4)(a) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` (`a run of test years` 3 2018 5000 0)
#ASSERT `s 44(4)(b) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least 25 calendar years, three of them in the last six` (`a run of test years` 25 1990 5000 0)
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(4)(b) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least 25 calendar years, three of them in the last six` (append (`a run of test years` 25 1980 5000 0) (`a run of test years` 4 2005 0 0))
#ASSERT `s 44(4)(c) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for each year after the month of cessation of the previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` (`a run of test years` 6 2015 5000 0) (JUST (YMD 2015 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(4)(c) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for each year after the month of cessation of the previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` (`a run of test years` 6 2015 5000 0) NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(4) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a post-retirement disability benefit` (`a run of test years` 6 2015 5000 0) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(4) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a post-retirement disability benefit` (`a run of test years` 3 2018 5000 0) NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(4) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a post-retirement disability benefit` (`a run of test years` 3 2018 5000 0) (JUST (YMD 2017 12 1))
-- subsection (5): no 1966 floor: born 15 June 1940, 18 deemed 1 July 1958; December 1965 is in the period
-- Arguments: month, date of birth, month determined disabled, excluded for disability, the month the benefit is payable for, family allowance recipient, the year's earnings, the basic exemption.
#ASSERT `s 44(5) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a post-retirement disability benefit` (YMD 1965 12 1) (YMD 1940 6 15) (YMD 2018 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2018 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(5) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a post-retirement disability benefit` (YMD 1958 6 1) (YMD 1940 6 15) (YMD 2018 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2018 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500
#ASSERT `s 44(5) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a post-retirement disability benefit` (YMD 1958 7 1) (YMD 1940 6 15) (YMD 2018 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2018 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500
#ASSERT `s 44(5) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a post-retirement disability benefit` (YMD 2018 5 1) (YMD 1940 6 15) (YMD 2018 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2018 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(5) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a post-retirement disability benefit` (YMD 2018 6 1) (YMD 1940 6 15) (YMD 2018 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2018 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(5) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a post-retirement disability benefit` (YMD 2000 6 1) (YMD 1940 6 15) (YMD 2018 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2018 6 1) FALSE 9000 3500
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(5) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a post-retirement disability benefit` (YMD 2000 6 1) (YMD 1940 6 15) (YMD 2018 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2018 6 1) TRUE 3000 3500
#ASSERT `s 44(5) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a post-retirement disability benefit` (YMD 2000 6 1) (YMD 1940 6 15) (YMD 2018 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2018 6 1) TRUE 3500 3500

§ `Tests -- the count-based rules (for the seat layer)`

#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(i) — at least four of the last six calendar years count, by number` 4
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(i) — at least four of the last six calendar years count, by number` 6
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(i) — at least four of the last six calendar years count, by number` 3
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — at least 25 calendar years count, three of them among the last six, by number` 25 3
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — at least 25 calendar years count, three of them among the last six, by number` 30 6
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — at least 25 calendar years count, three of them among the last six, by number` 24 6
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — at least 25 calendar years count, three of them among the last six, by number` 25 2
-- Arguments of (ii): there was a previous disability benefit that ceased, the included years from the cessation year on, how many of them count.
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — every calendar year since the previous disability benefit ceased counts, by number` TRUE 5 5
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — every calendar year since the previous disability benefit ceased counts, by number` TRUE 5 4
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — every calendar year since the previous disability benefit ceased counts, by number` FALSE 0 0
-- no included year since the cessation: every one of none counts
#ASSERT `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — every calendar year since the previous disability benefit ceased counts, by number` TRUE 0 0
#ASSERT `s 44(4)(a) — at least four of the last six calendar years count, by number` 4
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(4)(a) — at least four of the last six calendar years count, by number` 3
#ASSERT `s 44(4)(b) — at least 25 calendar years count, three of them among the last six, by number` 25 3
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(4)(b) — at least 25 calendar years count, three of them among the last six, by number` 25 2
#ASSERT `s 44(4)(c) — every calendar year since the previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceased counts, by number` TRUE 3 3
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(4)(c) — every calendar year since the previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceased counts, by number` TRUE 3 2
#ASSERT NOT `s 44(4)(c) — every calendar year since the previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceased counts, by number` FALSE 0 0
